{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/179872-from-genre-to-changeling","id":179872,"title":"From Genre to Changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-25T11:22:22-07:00","id":179872,"title":"From Genre to Changeling","content":"So we all know that given the proper set up, practically any other genre can be converted into a working Changeling: The Lost scenario. What kind of ideas do you guys think would make a suitable cross over?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Attack on Gentry:</b> Attack on Titan parody<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Premise A</b> - An army of Changelings have rebelled against their Keeper and are making a stand against his servants while desperately trying to make their way to the Hedge's exit.<br /> <br /> <b>Premise B</b> - One of the Gentry has a macro fetish and decides to amuse himself by destroying a city and devouring its residents. Having amassed hundreds of Changelings over the centuries, he sets his loyal followers loose upon the city one day and watches the carnage unfold.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Titan Shifters</b> - Ogre Seeming<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Military Police and the Nobility</b> - Fairest Seeming<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Recon Corp. and Garrison</b> - Wizened Seeming and Beast Seemings<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Titan Fodder and Civilians</b> - Darkling and Wizened Seeming<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>The Walls</b> - The Hedge<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Retaking the Walls</b> - Escaping the Hedge<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Common and Abnormal Titans</b> - The Gentry<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Colossal Titan</b> - Lord of the Domain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-30-2014, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T03:05:43-07:00","id":181794,"title":"","content":"Premise C An army of giant hobgoblins march out of the hedge and start eating people and breaking stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T12:39:55-07:00","id":182158,"title":"","content":"I think that would kind of destroy their whole cover if it takes place in the mundane world. Unless you mean they try to invade Arcadia itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-27T21:31:58-07:00","id":182575,"title":"","content":"Well I've yet to see this anime in question, but I believe that the premise is basically a giant apocalypse: humans are on the endangered species list and unfortunately if there's a Giants for the Ethical Treatment of Humans no one listens to them.<br /> <br /> So it wouldn't be like titan at all if the changelings could just skip across to the other side of the hedge to safety, if a changeling flees from the giants to say New York that shouldn't mean safety that should mean that the Giant has 8 million more people to eat while its there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T08:56:27-07:00","id":182934,"title":"","content":"Well the basic premise is this:<br /> <br /> 100 years ago, Titans appeared in the world and started devouring humans for no explainable reason. They can survive entirely on sunlight, so there's no biological need for them to eat humans. Over the century, humans were driven to the brink of extinction and now only one major city remains standing, protected by 3 walls spanning many miles in diameter so that humans have room to make villages and settlements. Humans have also devolved into a victorian steam punk era of technology having to rely on gas canisters, flintlock rifles, and black powder cannons to fend off the Titans. The walls are 50 meters tall, while most Titans don't reach higher than 20, so they've been safe. One day, a 60 meter Titan shows up at the gate, kicks that shit down, and vanishes before Titans storm through the first wall, massacring the people inside. Three years later, he shows up at the second gate to wreck their shit, but they manage to plug up the hole in time. The anime from then on is about them trying to retake the first wall from the invading Titans and plug up the hole.<br /> <br /> <br /> The series is still ongoing, but that's the plot for beginners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-28-2014, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T15:17:35-07:00","id":185152,"title":"","content":"Other candidates<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>American Mcgee's Alice:</b> The game is quite literally about madness and dreams and provides a perfect example of how the Gentry aren't the playful, compassionate Fairies you read about!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Silent Hill:</b> While I've never played Silent Hill, I believe that the core premise of the game is that the town is formed out of the dreams and subconscious of the story's protagonist and follows their road to recovery as they confront their inner demons. Could be a potential example of dealing with Clarity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Spyro the Dragon (original trilogy):</b> The games feature constantly traveling to different realms via portals and encountering beings who are being tormented by more powerful creatures for their simple amusement. The premise might focus on journeying to various Keeper realms and helping Lost escape their grasp.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Legend of Zelda:</b> With the Dungeon Masters as Keepers, Ganon as the domain's lord, and using Link and the Sages as the PC's, I think the Zelda series could work very well for a story about fighting back against the Gentry and liberating the realm from their control. Many events in the Zelda franchise are also quite morbid or Lost material if you think about it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-04T09:30:56-07:00","id":188036,"title":"","content":"Here's one I've never seen: Neil Gaiman's <i>Sandman</i>. The only real change/retcon I would make is to imply that Morpheus learned Clarity in <i>Preludes &amp; Nocturnes</i>, as Equinox Roads says occasionally happens to Actors trapped outside Arcadia too long. Puts a lot of the series in a whole new light, actually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-05T05:13:20-07:00","id":188641,"title":"","content":"Fables is a scenario I could see using to really freak out the players: a group of true fae exiles banding together to form their own community","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T20:28:17-07:00","id":198525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/179872-from-genre-to-changeling?p=188641#post188641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fables is a scenario I could see using to really freak out the players: a group of true fae exiles banding together to form their own community</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Among the Sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Perfect Durance story!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}